Ace Step 1.5 LoRA Training in ComfyUI

This repository contains my workflow, notes, and a quick-start guide for training LoRAs for ACE-Step 1.5 directly inside ComfyUI.

It’s not meant to be a perfect or official setup.
This is simply a practical base I’m sharing so you can experiment, modify it, and build your own workflows.

For the full implementation and complete documentation, check the original project:
https://github.com/filliptm/ComfyUI-FL-AceStep-Training

What this setup uses

This workflow is based on the ComfyUI-FL-AceStep-Training custom node pack, which provides a full LoRA training pipeline for ACE-Step 1.5 inside ComfyUI.

Main components:

ComfyUI
ACE-Step 1.5 model
ComfyUI-FL-AceStep-Training
Optional AceStep LLM Loader (for automatic dataset labeling)

From the checkpoint loader you will use:

MODEL
VAE
CLIP

Main nodes used

These are the core nodes from the original project:

FL AceStep LLM Loader
Loads a language model for optional automatic labeling.
FL AceStep Scan Audio Directory
Scans your dataset folder and reads metadata if available.
FL AceStep Auto-Label Samples
Generates captions, BPM, key, genre and other metadata.
FL AceStep Preprocess Dataset
Encodes audio with VAE and text with CLIP, then saves tensors (.pt).
FL AceStep Training Configuration
Lets you configure LoRA parameters like rank, alpha, dropout, learning rate, and epochs.
FL AceStep Train LoRA
Runs the actual training process.

Installation

Clone the original node repository into your ComfyUI custom nodes folder:

cd ComfyUI/custom_nodes
git clone https://github.com/filliptm/ComfyUI-FL-AceStep-Training.git

cd ComfyUI-FL-AceStep-Training
pip install -r requirements.txt

Restart ComfyUI after installation.

Quick workflow

Load the ACE-Step checkpoint
Scan your dataset folder
(Optional) Auto-label with LLM
Preprocess dataset into tensors
Configure training parameters
Train LoRA
Test the results

Notes

Dataset quality matters more than training time
Keep your dataset consistent (style, genre, structure)
Test with small runs before long training
LLM auto-labeling is optional

